{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And now send your livestock</b> etc. Why did Moses not warn Pharaoh at the plague of pestilence to say 'send your livestock,' as he did at the plague of hail? One may answer: he explained to him — send your livestock and fear the word of HaShem — in a lighter plague, and from it you may infer that the same was said for the severe one. Another interpretation: he did not warn him regarding pestilence because the pestilence was only upon the animals, whereas the hail struck both man and beast."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:43.248992379Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}